Chapter: GeoTruth
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Works chapter GopHandoff

 What geometry did the stub hand this payload, and was it still true when
 the payload got it?

 AMI Aptio V's GraphicsConsole is activated by the first real ConOut use,
 and that activation sets its own graphics mode. A stub that reads the GOP
 Mode->Info BEFORE its first ConOut call therefore publishes the splash
 mode's numbers for a scanout the firmware has since changed underneath it.
 That is the whole of the ASUS display corruption of 2026-08-02, and the
 firmware behaviour is the part we do not own and cannot derive.

 This prints the three published numbers and nothing else. It is the whole
 payload on purpose: the subject under test is the ORDER of two calls in
 build/cdx-to-pe.ps1, not any drawing code, and a probe that also painted
 could fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the question.

 The verdict is not readable from one run. build/boot/test-conout-remode.ps1
 boots this twice, with codex-vm's -uefi-conout-remode on and off, and the
 assertion is that the two arms DISAGREE in the specific way a live re-mode
 produces. Either arm alone is satisfied by a payload printing a constant.

Section: Probe

  opening : Nothing -> [Console] Nothing
  opening (dummy) =
    let w = boot-fb-w 0
    in let h = boot-fb-h 0
    in let stride = boot-fb-stride 0
    in print-line-uni ("GEOTRUTH w=" & show w & " h=" & show h & " stride=" & show stride)
